# Seasonal Discovery — featured picks & collections

## Universal litmus test (every theme)

Apply this before adding **any** seasonal pick (Hello Fall, Halloween, Holiday, rainy-day, etc.):

> **If it isn’t special because of this season / this month, don’t make it a seasonal pick.**

Ask: *Would I specially recommend this because it’s fall / Halloween / holidays — or would I recommend it any ordinary month?*

| Answer | Action |
|--------|--------|
| Special **because of the season** | Eligible for seasonal collection / featured / seasonal badge |
| Good anytime (recurring yoga, FIT4MOM, weekly storytime, music class, generic open house) | Keep in **regular browse** only (Parent & Me, Stories, Festivals, etc.) |

Seasonal Discovery must read as **curated editorial**, not a month dump of every good activity.

### Shared principles (all themes)

- Prioritize events **genuinely good for ages 0–5**.
- Keep each collection tight (**~6–8**); Home carousel **max 4** active featured picks (one horizontal row; scrollable on mobile).
- **Rotate** time-sensitive festivals into featured windows near their dates; drop when the window ends or the date passes.
- Recurring / enrollment / year-round Parent & Me, Stories, Music → **never** seasonal editorial by default.
- Community one-offs with a **weak seasonal tie** → regular Festivals / Browse, not seasonal picks.
- Leaving featured does **not** remove an activity from the collection; only drop from `collectionEventIds` / `driveEventIds` when it no longer belongs in the theme.

### Seasonal badge scope (all themes)

- **One live theme only.** Fall Pick and Halloween Pick never appear at the same time. Badge label follows `getActiveSeasonalCollection()` — same source as the Home band and “See all” collection.
- While **Hello, Fall** is active → curated members show **Fall Pick** only.
- When the theme swaps to **Halloween with little ones** → drop Fall Pick everywhere; eligible curated members show **Halloween Pick**.
- The **same event** may stay featured across the swap if it still fits (e.g. pumpkin farm: Fall Pick in September → Halloween Pick in October). List it in both themes’ `collectionEventIds` / `driveEventIds`.
- Events that leave the active theme stay in **regular browse** but **lose** the seasonal badge.
- Badge = membership in the **active** theme’s collection/drive IDs — not title heuristics.
- **Seasonal Discovery surfaces** (collection page + home seasonal band): **no** seasonal badge — the page/band already is the theme. Pass `seasonalEditorial={false}` on cards there.
- **Everywhere else** (browse list, browse map, home results, nearby, city landing): show the active theme badge. `BrowseEventCard` and `EventCard` default `seasonalEditorial` **on**.

### Browse date window

Public discovery shows roughly the **next 60 days** (`PUBLIC_DISPLAY_WINDOW_DAYS` in `src/utils/dates.ts`). From early September that reaches **~end of October** (~10/30). Fall and Halloween inventory can both appear in Browse; only one seasonal **module + badge** is editorial at a time.

