## Three layers (do not collapse)

| Layer | Field | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| **Featured** | `featuredWindows` | Home carousel — **temporary** (~2–3 weeks per pick) |
| **Collection** | `collectionEventIds` | Full “See all” close-to-home set — **season-long** while valid |
| **Drive** | `driveEventIds` | “Worth a little drive” — **stable** anchors; rotate less often |

### Geographic rule (drive / out-of-area)

> **Regular Browse = Palo Alto · Los Altos · Mountain View · Sunnyvale only.**

Out-of-area farms/festivals/trains belong in **`driveEventIds`** (Hidden seasonal drive events) — never Go live into the public sheet/Browse feed. Admin Discovery may still hold `Regional ·` review rows; Approve/Go live for non-core cities is blocked.

## Featured rotation

- Default featured duration: **~2–3 weeks** per pick.
- Rotate **at least 1–2 cards every ~2 weeks** so the carousel stays fresh.
- Keep the Home carousel to a **tight, intentional set** of active `featuredWindows` for the day — no hard card-count cap. Prefer `anchor: true`, then editorial order in `featuredWindows`.
- **Home band order:** prioritize events happening **today**, then soonest next day / start time (`sortSeasonalDiscoveryEvents`).
- Resolve with Pacific calendar date (`zonedCalendarDate`) so evening PT does not flip windows early via UTC.
- Mark **1–2 anchor slots** (`anchor: true`) — festival weekends, strong seasonal rows.
- Use `note` on each window for launch-review context.
- Resolve Home carousel with `resolveFeaturedSeasonalEvents()` / `getFeaturedEventIdsForDate()` — **never** a static ID list.
- Home band layout: **one horizontal line** (desktop cards across; mobile horizontal scroll). Do not wrap to a multi-row grid.

## Theme transitions

- **One seasonal theme module at a time** — `activeFrom` / `activeUntil` do not overlap.
- Home band, collection CTA, and card badges all use `getActiveSeasonalCollection()`.
- **Transition week:** blend **1–2 picks from the next theme** into the current theme’s `featuredWindows` before the module title swaps (preview on the outgoing theme; badge stays the outgoing theme’s label until `activeUntil` ends).
- After the swap, remove outgoing-theme IDs that no longer fit; keep spanning picks (farms, etc.) on the incoming collection so their badge label updates.

### Timing (2026)

| Theme | Live window |
|-------|-------------|
| Hello, Fall | ~Sep 1 – Oct 5 (early–late September through Diwali / Mid-Autumn weekend) |
| Halloween with little ones | Oct 6 – Oct 31 (once Halloween inventory is ready; browse window still reaches ~10/30 from early Sep) |

## Drive picks

- Special outings **outside core cities** — not every farm needs a drive slot.
- Prefer **1–2 stable drive anchors** per theme.
- Do not duplicate next-theme drive picks in the current collection long-term — preview in transition only.

## Adding a new seasonal pick (checklist)

1. Pass the **universal litmus test** for this theme.
2. Ensure the event exists in catalog (sheet, staging, or `seasonal*DriveEvents.ts`).
3. Add to **`collectionEventIds`** (close to home) or **`driveEventIds`** (worth a drive) — not both unless intentional.
4. Add **`featuredWindows`** only when spotlighting on Home for a specific period.
5. Update **`SEASONAL_THEME_SCHEDULE`** if theme dates or transition notes change.
6. Verify on `/experiment/seasonal-launch-review`; confirm badges stay off on seasonal surfaces.

